###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Maximum errors, range-normalised errors and log(1 - R2) (Table 2) are not encoded. Hellinger distances for pressure, molecular fraction, diffusion and RDF (Table 1, Table SI2) score MD-derived properties, not energy/force errors. Yukawa and Tersoff are reparametrised empirical potentials.
# - MLIP hyperparameters are in the SI; the training-set size is not stated in the main text.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bischoff2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

